meta {
  name: 6. Self-Register as Driver While TORG_ADMIN (Rejected)
  type: http
  seq: 6
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/driver-app/license
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{accessToken}}
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "name": "{{driverName}}",
    "licenseNumber": "{{driverLicenseNumber}}",
    "dateOfBirth": "{{driverDob}}"
  }
}

docs {
  Negative case for UserRoleValidator: the same "Register Driver (Self-Onboard)" call as
  driver-onboarding step 3 (POST /api/driver-app/license, DriverService.createDriverSelf), but
  made with the TORG_ADMIN's own token instead of a driver's.

  Run this right after step 2 in THIS flow (Verify OTP as Torg Admin) — it needs {{accessToken}}
  to be the torg admin's, not a driver's. Steps 3/4/5 don't touch {{accessToken}}, so running
  this after them is also fine as long as driver-onboarding's own verify-otp hasn't re-run since.

  Before the role-transition fix, this silently created a Driver record linked to the torg
  admin's own User row (their role was left untouched, but the Driver→User link still happened) —
  the exact bug this flow now guards against.

  Expected: 400, "User with role TORG_ADMIN cannot be assigned role DRIVER". No Driver record
  should be created for the torg admin's phone — confirm via GET /api/drivers/user/{userId} (see
  the plutus-api collection) if you want to double-check no row appeared.
}
